[TestRequireAsyncDisposable/invalid-1 - 1]
Diagnostic 1: mustClose (9:3 - 11:3)
Message: '[Symbol.asyncDispose]' must 'await this.close()' so the AbortController is aborted and in-flight work settles.
Help: Add 'await this.close();' to the method.
   8 | class Service extends ADisposable {
   9 |   async [Symbol.asyncDispose](): Promise<void> {
     |   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  10 |     await work();
     | ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  11 |   }
     | ~~~
  12 | }
---

[TestRequireAsyncDisposable/invalid-2 - 1]
Diagnostic 1: closeOnce (12:11 - 12:22)
Message: '[Symbol.asyncDispose]' must call 'this.close()' exactly once: the second call throws, because close() rejects a disposal that already happened.
Help: Delete this call and keep the first one.
  11 |     await work();
  12 |     await this.close();
     |           ~~~~~~~~~~~~
  13 |   }
---

[TestRequireAsyncDisposable/invalid-3 - 1]
Diagnostic 1: noTrack (10:11 - 10:28)
Message: 'this.track()' does nothing inside '[Symbol.asyncDispose]': the await already waits for the promise, and after close() the in-flight set is cleared, so nothing will ever drain it.
Help: Await the promise directly, without wrapping it in track().
   9 |   async [Symbol.asyncDispose](): Promise<void> {
  10 |     await this.track(work());
     |           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  11 |     await this.close();
---

[TestRequireAsyncDisposable/invalid-4 - 1]
Diagnostic 1: noTrack (10:11 - 10:34)
Message: 'this.track()' does nothing inside '[Symbol.asyncDispose]': the await already waits for the promise, and after close() the in-flight set is cleared, so nothing will ever drain it.
Help: Await the promise directly, without wrapping it in track().
